@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "DevErrorAssistant Demo";
}

<div class="text-center py-5">
    <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3">DevErrorAssistant Demo Application</h1>
    <p class="lead text-muted mb-4">
        Demonstrates the <code>DevErrorAssistant</code> package with developer diagnostics and optional Groq AI explanations.
    </p>

    <div class="card shadow-sm mx-auto p-4 mb-4" style="max-width: 680px; text-align: left;">
        <h5 class="card-title text-danger">1. Test Unhandled Runtime Exception</h5>
        <p class="card-text text-secondary">
            Click below to invoke <code>/Home/ThrowError</code>. This endpoint deliberately throws an unhandled
            <code>System.InvalidOperationException</code> to demonstrate the custom error page, collapsible stack trace, and AI explanation.
        </p>
        <div class="d-flex gap-2 mb-3">
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="ThrowError" class="btn btn-danger">
                Trigger Test Exception
            </a>
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Privacy" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
                Normal Page (Privacy)
            </a>
        </div>
        <small class="text-muted">
            <em>Note: If no Groq API key is configured, the application degrades gracefully: the full diagnostic page displays, and the AI card clearly notes that the API key is not configured. The app will never crash due to a missing key.</em>
        </small>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm mx-auto p-4" style="max-width: 680px; text-align: left; background-color: #f8fafc; border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1;">
        <h5 class="card-title text-primary">2. Local AI Configuration (.NET User Secrets)</h5>
        <p class="card-text text-secondary" style="font-size: 0.95rem;">
            To test live AI explanations locally without exposing your secret, configure User Secrets from your terminal:
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded" style="font-size: 0.85rem; overflow-x: auto;">dotnet user-secrets set "Groq:ApiKey" "YOUR_GROQ_API_KEY" --project DevErrorAssistant.Demo</pre>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
            <strong>Security Rule:</strong> Never commit API keys or secret files to git. User Secrets are stored securely outside the repository directory.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
